---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import ContactModal from '../../components/Contactmodal.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/index.js';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';

const lang = 'en';
const strings = t(lang);

const introParagraphs = [
  `The <em>Historical Atlas of China</em> (中國歷史地圖集)<sup id="fnref1"><a href="#fn1">1</a></sup> is a multi-volume work compiled by Tan Qixiang in the 1980s. While <u><a href="https://history-map.osgeo.cn/#/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">some websites</a></u> have overlaid scanned sections of the atlas onto modern basemaps, I'm not aware of any effort to translate and digitise its contents into a structured, topography-integrated database. This project aims to fill that gap.`,
  `Below is a short Q&A outlining the key stylistic choices and conventions I've adopted in this project.`
];

const qna = [
  {
    icon: 'ti-book-2',
    question: `Why use Tan Qixiang's Historical Atlas of China? Should I trust these maps?`,
    answer: [
      `Tan Qixiang's <em>Historical Atlas of China</em> is the most authoritative atlas of Chinese history and remains a standard reference for historical geography.<sup id="fnref2"><a href="#fn2">2</a></sup>`,
      `Like all historical cartography, however, the atlas inevitably involves approximation and informed interpretation. Compiled in the 1980s, before the advent of comprehensive digital datasets and improved access to historical sources and far-flung places, some errors and uncertainties are unavoidable. The maps should not be read as a perfectly accurate reconstruction, but it remains among the best available estimates of where places were located and what their surrounding landscapes looked like.`
    ]
  },
  {
    icon: 'ti-map-question',
    question: `Why are some locations from Romance of the Three Kingdoms, games, or historical texts missing?`,
    answer: [
      `These maps reflect the administrative geography of the 260s, while games and the <em>Romance of the Three Kingdoms</em> often focus on earlier parts of the era. By the 260s, many counties and towns had been merged, abolished, renamed, or had fallen out of use.`,
      `Additionally, some locations featured in stories or games are fictional, or have been conflated with later place names, and are therefore not represented on these maps.`
    ]
  },
  {
    icon: 'ti-affiliate',
    question: `How does this project modify or build on Tan Qixiang's maps?`,
    answer: [
      `This project georeferences Tan's maps with modern towns and cities that also appear in the original atlas, using them as anchor points for alignment. Topography from HydroSHEDS<sup id="fnref3"><a href="#fn3">3</a></sup> has been incorporated to provide elevation context.`,
      `In some cases, rivers in the original atlas do not align with valleys in the modern topography. Where possible, they have been adjusted to follow thenearest plausible valley, while preserving their overall course. Where no convincing correspondence exists, they have been left as originally drawn. These adjustments are necessarily approximate, as river courses may have shifted significantly since antiquity, particularly across lowland floodplains.  Even so, the integration of elevation data should provide a closer approximation of the overall landscape.`
    ]
  },
  {
    icon: 'ti-language',
    question: `How were pronunciations for names determined?`,
    answer: [
      `In most cases, the standard modern Hanyu Pinyin system is used. For more obscure or ambiguous names, I traced the root meaning of the characters and matched them with the most appropriate modern Pinyin pronunciation.`,
      `One example is Jianwei/Qianwei. Today, the town is known as Qianwei (犍為), and indeed the first character is usually given only the Qian- pronunciation. However, in Han-period records and artefacts the commandery appears as Jianwei (楗為), with a wood radical (木) rather than a cow radical (牛).<sup id="fnref4"><a href="#fn4">4</a></sup> <sup id="fnref5"><a href="#fn5">5</a></sup> <sup id="fnref6"><a href="#fn6">6</a></sup>  At some point after the Han, the character and its pronunciation somehow shifted. In the maps, both pronunciations are included for accessibility, since it is unclear whether the change had already occurred by the Three Kingdoms period.`,
      `Inevitably, some cases may have been overlooked or interpreted differently. If you notice any errors or have questions about particular names or locations, please don't hesitate to get in touch.`
    ]
  },
  {
    icon: 'ti-ripple',
    question: `What qualifies as a canal, and what does not?`,
    answer: [
      `Generally, waterways with the character 渠 (<i>qu</i>, "canal") in their names can be identified as canals, since these were deliberately constructed or engineered channels. In flatter, agriculturally intensive regions, especially downstream of the Yellow River, the distinction becomes less clear. Existing channels were often excavated, altered, redirected, or reinforced to serve irrigation and transport purposes, effectively functioning as canals even if not entirely man-made`,
      `For this project, I have included only the major canal-rivers. I have not explicitly marked their many tributaries and connecting channels as canals, though they were most likely part of the broader network.`
    ]
  }
];

const references = [
  {
    id: 'fn1',
    refId: 'fnref1',
    html: `Tan, Qixiang. <em>Historical Atlas of China</em> (中國歷史地圖集). Beijing: China Cartographic Publishing House, 1982-1988.`
  },
  {
    id: 'fn2',
    refId: 'fnref2',
    html: `Wilkinson, Endymion. <em>Chinese History: A New Manual</em>. Cambridge, MA: Harvard University Asia Center, 2013, p. 245.`
  },
  {
    id: 'fn3',
    refId: 'fnref3',
    html: `Lehner, Bernhard, K. Verdin, and A. Jarvis. "New Global Hydrography Derived from Spaceborne Elevation Data." <em>Eos, Transactions, American Geophysical Union</em> 89, no. 10 (2008): 93-94. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1029/2008EO100001" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://doi.org/10.1029/2008EO100001</a>.`
  },
  {
    id: 'fn4',
    refId: 'fnref4',
    html: `Shimen Eulogy Rubbing (石門頌《司隸校尉楅為楊君頌》拓本). Wikimedia Commons, last modified 2023, <a href="https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%9F%B3%E9%97%A8%E9%A2%82" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/石门颂</a>.`
  },
  {
    id: 'fn5',
    refId: 'fnref5',
    html: `Tong Chun-fung (唐俊峰). "The Organization and Administration of Tianguan in Hexi during the Western Han Dynasty." <em>Journal of the Institute of Chinese Culture</em> (《中國文化研究所學報》), no. 59 (July 2014): 87-120. <a href="https://doi.org/10.29708/JCS.CUHK.201407_(59).0004" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://doi.org/10.29708/JCS.CUHK.201407_(59).0004</a>.`
  },
  {
    id: 'fn6',
    refId: 'fnref6',
    html: `Ni Tao. <em>A Record of One of the Six Arts</em>, vol. 53 (《六藝之一錄》卷五十三). Chinese Text Project. <a href="https://ctext.org/wiki.pl?if=gb&chapter=79374" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://ctext.org/wiki.pl?if=gb&chapter=79374</a>.`
  }
];
---

<Base title={`About: Three Kingdom Maps · ${strings.siteTitle}`} lang={lang}>
  <div class="site about-site">
    <Nav lang={lang} strings={strings} />

    <main class="about-maps-page">
      <header class="about-header">
        <div class="breadcrumb">
          <a href={url('/maps')} class="bc-link">Maps</a>
          <span class="bc-sep">&rsaquo;</span>
          <a href={url('/maps/map-overall')} class="bc-link">Map of the Three Kingdoms</a>
          <span class="bc-sep">&rsaquo;</span>
          <span class="bc-cur">About: Three Kingdom Maps</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="page-title">About: Three Kingdom Maps</h1>
      </header>
      <section class="intro-section">
        {introParagraphs.map(paragraph => <p set:html={paragraph} />)}
      </section>

      <section class="qna-section" aria-label="Map questions and answers">
        {qna.map((item) => (
          <details class="qna-item">
            <summary>
              <span class="qna-icon"><i class={`ti ${item.icon}`} aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
              <span class="qna-question">{item.question}</span>
              <i class="ti ti-chevron-down qna-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="qna-answer">
              {item.answer.map(paragraph => <p set:html={paragraph} />)}
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </section>

      <section class="references-section" aria-labelledby="references-title">
        <div class="section-heading-row references-heading">
          <h2 id="references-title">References</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="references-list">
          {references.map((reference) => (
            <li id={reference.id}>
              <span set:html={reference.html} />
              <a class="ref-back" href={`#${reference.refId}`} aria-label="Back to note">&#8617;</a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>
    </main>

    <ContactModal lang={lang} strings={strings} />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-site {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 84% 0%, rgba(196,154,94,0.12), transparent 30rem),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #10100f 0%, #080808 54%, #0d0d0d 100%);
  }

  .about-maps-page {
    max-width: 1500px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.2rem clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem) 3.5rem;
  }

  .about-header {
    padding: 1.25rem 0 1.1rem;
    border-bottom: 0.5px solid rgba(196,154,94,0.22);
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .bc-link {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #d5ad6b;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .bc-link:hover {
    color: #f0d39a;
  }

  .bc-sep {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: rgba(232,221,202,0.35);
  }

  .bc-cur {
    color: rgba(232,221,202,0.66);
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 42px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #f2eadc;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .intro-section {
    max-width: 1500px;
    padding: 1.55rem 0 1.15rem;
  }

  .intro-section p {
    font-size: 17px;
  }


  .qna-answer p,
  .references-list li {
    color: #d6d1c4;
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.78;
  }

  .intro-section sup,
  .qna-answer sup {
    font-size: 0.6em;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .intro-section :global(sup a),
  .qna-answer :global(sup a) {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .intro-section :global(a),
  .qna-answer :global(a),
  .references-list :global(a),
  .references-list .ref-back {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(214, 209, 196, 0.35);
    text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
  }

  .intro-section :global(a:hover),
  .qna-answer :global(a:hover),
  .references-list :global(a:hover),
  .references-list .ref-back:hover {
    color: #f0d39a;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(240, 211, 154, 0.55);
  }

  .intro-section p + p,
  .qna-answer p + p {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    box-shadow: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-item {
    border: 0.5px solid rgba(196,154,94,0.2);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(12, 12, 11, 0.72);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 48px rgba(0,0,0,0.22);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-item summary {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    min-height: 62px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.05rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #ede6d7;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    color: #d6ad6b;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-icon i {
    font-size: 1.32rem;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-question {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-chevron {
    color: rgba(232,221,202,0.54);
    transition: transform 180ms ease;
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-item[open] .qna-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .about-maps-page .qna-answer {
    padding: 0 1.1rem 1.2rem 4rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    max-width: 1280px;
  }

  .about-maps-page .references-section {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1.35rem 0 0;
    border: 0;
    border-top: 0.5px solid rgba(196,154,94,0.25);
    background: transparent;
    box-shadow: none;
  }

  .references-heading {
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }

  .references-heading h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading-en);
    color: #d6ad6b;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.3vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .references-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .references-list li {
    padding-left: 0.25rem;
    color: #bfb6a5;
    font-size: 0.83rem;
  }

  .references-list li::marker {
    color: #d6ad6b;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .ref-back {
    margin-left: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 840px) {
    .about-maps-page {
      padding: 1rem 1rem 2.5rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .about-header {
      padding-top: 1rem;
    }

    .page-title {
      font-size: 2.7rem;
    }

    .intro-section {
      padding: 1.25rem 0 1rem;
    }

    .about-maps-page .qna-item summary {
      gap: 0.6rem;
      padding: 0.8rem 0.85rem;
      min-height: 58px;
    }

    .about-maps-page .qna-icon {
      width: 1.55rem;
      height: 1.55rem;
    }

    .about-maps-page .qna-icon i {
      font-size: 1.08rem;
    }

    .about-maps-page .qna-question {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .about-maps-page .qna-answer {
      padding: 0 0.9rem 1rem 0.9rem;
    }
  }
</style>
